WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Today is day two of the Bridesmaid Proposal series.

00:02.000 --> 00:09.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
A series where I show you unique Bridesmaid Proposal gift ideas that aren't full of a bunch of junk they're gonna throw away anyways, and are budget friendly.

00:09.000 --> 00:12.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Today we're going with like a disco cowgirl theme.

00:12.000 --> 00:13.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Think Nashville Bachelor at party.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
We're putting together a cute little cocktail kit.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
This is me taking everything out of the box because I forgot to put cute tool in there to jush up the inside.

00:20.000 --> 00:22.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
And crime against humanity, I know.

00:22.000 --> 00:28.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
I threw in these cute craft mix drink packets, but obviously you can put in whatever cocktail mix suits your fancy.

00:28.000 --> 00:31.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
I added a little card that's gonna match the front of the box, and then is that shot glass?

00:31.000 --> 00:33.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Not the cutest thing you've ever seen.

00:33.000 --> 00:34.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
I mean, come on. Are you freaking kidding me?

00:34.000 --> 00:39.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Then the kit comes with these cute custom Bridesmaid Proposal stickers, so I'm adding one of those to the front window.

00:39.000 --> 00:45.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
I love it because it still gives off that really personalized look that you see on like Etsy and Pinterest, but it's not a million dollars.

00:45.000 --> 00:49.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Then we're finally bringing back the JoJo Siwa approved giant tool bow for the front.

00:49.000 --> 00:55.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
I layered two types of pink and white to make it super fluffy and obnoxious, and then hot glued that puppy onto the front of the box.

00:55.000 --> 01:01.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
Of course, we had to drive the theme home with a matching pink vodka bottle, and look how freaking cute this turned out.

01:01.000 --> 01:03.000 line:16 position:50% size:80% align:middle
So unique, I'm obsessed.
